+/* Freed contiguous memory waits for the GPU.
+ *
+ * The pushbuffer runs on the poll thread, behind the title by up to a frame
+ * (the flip pacing sleeps there). A title that draws a texture, frees it and
+ * loads the next one into the same pages before the GPU got to the draw has
+ * the draw sample the next texture's bytes. On hardware the GPU keeps up and
+ * D3D blocks on busy resources; here it did not. Deathrow's Tonight's Game
+ * screen drew its 512x512 backdrop and its 256x256 panel from the pages its
+ * 512x128 ad had just been loaded into -- three textures, one physical page,
+ * one frame.
+ *
+ * So a freed block keeps its pages until the poll thread has executed a
+ * pushbuffer segment the title kicked off after the free. That kick covers
+ * every draw written before the free. Counting kicks: at the free the poll
+ * thread has picked up g_pb_kicks_seen new PUT values. The next one may have
+ * been read before the free, and the one after may be the value that was
+ * already in the register then; the third is a PUT written after the free.
+ * So the block is released once g_pb_kicks_done reaches that count + 3.
+ *
+ * A held block is no longer a block (a second free of it is ignored) but its
+ * pages stay in use. An allocation that would fail releases every held block
+ * and tries again, so holding never turns into running out. Off with
+ * RECOMP_CONTIG_DEFER=0, and idle until the poll thread has seen a kick (no
+ * pushbuffer walk, nothing to wait for). Caller holds the arena lock. */
+#define CONTIG_DEFER_MAX 16384
